    "text": "cozadlocal.com\nwebsite\nCozad\nComeca to Host 75th Anniversary Free Cookout\nBy Ellen Mortensen,\n9 hours agoThe year 1950 marked the beginning of the Korean War for America, as the country was still reeling from World War II, which had ended only a few short years earlier. It was a time when many were looking for some type of peace and solitude; a place where they could escape images of war, even for just a short time. Rev. Adrian J. Edgar had a vision for just such a place, and with the help of other members of the Cozad United Methodist Church, established Camp Comeca.",
